{"name":"Skylight","hex":"#b8d6d7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skylight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A window, dome, or opening in the roof or ceiling, to admit natural light.","Diffuse sky radiation—solar radiation reaching the earth's surface after having been scattered from the direct solar beam by molecules or suspensoids in the atmosphere."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skylight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skylight","blocks":[{"text":"A skylight is a light-permitting structure or window, usually made of glass or translucent plastic, that forms all or part of the roof space of a building for daylighting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Cupula_do_Centro_Cultural_Banco_do_Brasil_%28Rio_de_Janeiro%29.jpg/330px-Cupula_do_Centro_Cultural_Banco_do_Brasil_%28Rio_de_Janeiro%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylight"},{"title":"Skylight (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Skylight is a play by British dramatist David Hare. The play premiered in the West End at the Royal National Theatre in 1995, moving to the Wyndham's Theatre in 1996. After opening on Broadway in 1996, it played again in the West End in 1997 at the Vaudeville Theatre. It was revived at Wyndham's Theatre in the West End in 2014, and that production transferred to Broadway in 2015."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Skylight_%28play_-_cover_art_of_bound_edition_of_script%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylight_(play)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG/500px-Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG/1280px-Inter